{"agent_id":"pp3g-5cWX-implementation-task-for-issue-344-apply-the-approved","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-10T03:14:53.530029256Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"484eb300-79b2-4baa-99c7-f5f831f27952","comment_uuid":"8cf95e81-0cfc-43bf-a0eb-24c618cbc3b8","author":"pp3g-5cWX-implementation-task-for-issue-344-apply-the-approved","content":"# Result: #342 deny-by-default boundary applied (band-aid) — #344\n\n**Status**: DONE. All 4 change-set files edited, verified, committed.\n\n## Changes (commit c4072f04, ref [#342])\n\n1. **`.opencode/agents/reviewer.md`** — removed `opencode *`, `cargo *`, `npm *`; replaced `git *` with the 8 read-only prefixes (`git status/diff/log/show`, `git branch -a/-r/-vv/--show-current`); replaced `rtk *` with the 7 read-only proxies (`rtk read/ls/tree/grep/find/wc/diff`); fixed `\"crosslink sync\"` → `\"crosslink sync *\"`.\n2. **`.opencode/agents/auditor.md`** — same minus cargo/npm (auditor never had them).\n3. **`.opencode/permissions.md`** — both snapshot rows (Reviewer, Auditor) updated to the new exact maps; rationale text updated.\n4. **`.crosslink/hook-config.json` §2.8** — removed the 12 code-exec prefixes (`opencode `, `cargo test/build/check/clippy/fmt`, `npm test/run`, `npx `, `tsc`, `node `, `python `) from the global `allowed_bash_prefixes`; moved them to `agent_overrides.by_type.builder.allowed_bash_prefixes` so builders keep the pass-through. All read-only prefixes kept in the global list (crosslink, git read, jj read, ls/dir/pwd/echo, rtk read, ps/pgrep/tmux, grep/tail/head/wc/stat/diff/free/df/uptime/date/which/env, git worktree list, git -C, curl -I/--head).\n\n## Verification (proposal §5)\n\n**Static**: both frontmatters parse as YAML; allow sets are the exact §2 tables (25 allows + `\"*\": deny` each — asserted set-equality); excluded commands (`opencode *`, `git *`, `cargo *`, `npm *`, `rtk *`, literal `crosslink sync`) absent from both agent files and the permissions.md snapshot rows; hook-config.json parses; global list keeps all read-only prefixes; `by_type.builder.allowed_bash_prefixes` holds exactly the 12 moved prefixes.\n\n**Matcher (positive/negative)**: wrote a bun script using the fork's **actual** `Wildcard.match` (core/src/util/wildcard.ts) and the exact `evaluate`/`fromConfig` semantics (permission/index.ts). For BOTH reviewer and auditor rulesets: all 25 §5 positive commands ALLOW (incl. bare `git status`, `ls`, `cat`, `rtk read`, `crosslink issue show 342`, `crosslink issue comment 342 ...`, and bare `crosslink sync` — the `sync *` pattern fix is confirmed working); all 16 negative commands DENY (`opencode run --pure/--auto`, `git config core.hooksPath`, `git update-ref`, `git checkout main`, `git restore <file>`, `git rm`, `git branch <name>`, `git stash create`, `git fetch origin main:main`, `cargo run/build/test`, `npm run/test`, `npx x`, `tsc`, `node`, `python`, `rtk gh/docker/summary/kubectl/wget/git`). Full script source + output available on request (kept at /tmp/opencode/perm-verify.ts).\n\n**Escape regression**: `opencode run --pure --agent builder` → **deny** at Layer 1 for both roles (matcher-level test using the fork's exact matcher; no live reviewer session spawned — reviewer/auditor role is task-denied from a builder session, so the Layer-1 matcher test is the faithful proxy, and Layer 1 is the load-bearing boundary per proposal §0.3).\n\n**Workflow regression**: orchestrator.md and builder.md untouched (`git diff` empty). Builder retains full bash — Layer 1 `bash: allow` unchanged, `by_type.builder.allowed_bash_prefixes` restores the plugin-layer pass-through, and agent tracking_mode is relaxed (plugin section 7 allows any non-blocked-git command regardless). Plugin-layer merge simulation confirms builder gets the code-exec pass-throughs while reviewer/auditor get none from the plugin layer. This live builder session continued to function (bash, git, crosslink comments/sync) against the new hook-config.\n\n## Findings / residuals\n\n- **Matcher semantics confirmed at source**: `Wildcard.match` (core/src/util/wildcard.ts:11) rewrites a trailing ` *` to `( .*)?`, so `\"git status *\"` matches bare `git status` — the whole §2 allowlist convention is sound. `evaluate` uses `findLast`, so later specific allows beat the leading `\"*\": deny`.\n- **`crosslink sync` literal-pattern bug (auditor finding) is fixed**: bare `crosslink sync` now matches `\"crosslink sync *\"` → allow (confirmed by matcher test).\n- **Residual (not in change set)**: crosslink-guard.ts's `DEFAULT_ALLOWED_BASH` fallback still lists code-exec prefixes, but it is only used when hook-config.json is absent; our repo always provides the sanitized global list, which replaces it (crosslink-guard.ts:387-389). Plugin source change deliberately out of scope for this band-aid.\n- **Band-aid framing honored**: no opencode source changed; boundary lives at the permission layer (Layer 1) as the proposal prescribes. Research questions (microVMs/Containers) remain open per #344.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: live reviewer/auditor session spawn (blocked by role separation); orchestrator live session spawn; the `.kickoff-session` and `.crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref` working-tree artifacts were intentionally left out of the commit (prior permission commits set that precedent).","created_at":"2026-08-10T03:14:53.519732831Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:p6XLq5bUTJioISc4Vbku+DjeNby0lZ5qlJOvg6uIOoU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4PE06/YrWfEShgxsiHB23bwwFb4/TEFHS6uIkxrRYTEAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAl9nNqbpOCPBn5rDR3Po7bpQTc7FJZaVlfPBNtBmVBM+P/QMTon4UM0xuItZyGGMIhlM5nZCD7IPm+m89IKxbBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:p6XLq5bUTJioISc4Vbku+DjeNby0lZ5qlJOvg6uIOoU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4PE06/YrWfEShgxsiHB23bwwFb4/TEFHS6uIkxrRYTEAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHa0SmiVqpRSknjO1l+l7F9Q6iXNsvN/zqqpmKabt1f2+x2Vly2G33j